WEBVTT

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.970
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:34.210
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:39.050
Calling everything delicious!

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:43.550
The more I eat, the more powerful I get!

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.920
Let’s capture ingredients around the world!

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.500
I dream of being an invincible 
Gourmet Fighter!!

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.530
Now on to the bottom of the 
sea, or the tops of glaciers!

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:59.200
Jump! Jump Jump Jump! 
Knock! Knock Knock Knock!

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.400
Give thanks!

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.610
Let’s eat!

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.410
Wow wo!! Spiked Punch! Wow wo!! Multi-fold!

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:15.550
Guts! Gutsy Guts! I can eat any dream!

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:20.820
Wow wo!! My very own... 
Wow wo!! ...Full Course!

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.990
Guts! Gutsy Guts! Gather them all up!

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:31.070
And put the world on my plate!

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.870
Wow wow wow! Eat the mountains!!

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.440
Wow wow wow! Toriko!!

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.040
Wow wow wow! Eat the oceans!!

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:43.310
Wow wow wow! Tori, Tori, Tori, Toriko!!

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.490
Someone once said...

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.390
There is fluffy, strongly sweet

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:56.260
melon-flavored cotton candy fruit...

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:00.060
Cottamelon Candy!

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.970
There is fragrant natto that 
has a first-rate flavor,

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:07.300
possesses a wonderful stickiness,

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:11.140
and sparkles like platinum...

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:14.510
Platinatto!

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:18.510
The world is in the Gourmet Age...

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:23.350
An age in which people quest for 
yet unknown culinary delights!

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.350
In order to get Mellow Cola, Toriko,

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:30.020
Komatsu, and Zebra headed to the Sand Garden.

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:33.730
Along the way, Zebra warned Komatsu.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:39.300
Any animals that can't adapt to 
me well will end up goin' extinct.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:43.100
They arrived at the Sand Garden.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:46.870
There, Komatsu expressed his dissatisfaction 
at having Zebra along with them.

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:51.510
However, the denizens of a 
desert town idolized Zebra.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:55.350
And then, an Eight-Tailed 
Scorpion suddenly appeared,

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:57.680
but was defeated by Zebra's Voice Cutter.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:04.990
Komatsu Disappears! 
Devilish Desert Labyrinth!

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:12.230
Well, saddle up two camels for us.

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:12.970
Okay!

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.040
Hey, kid!

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:20.040
I heard what you said!

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:23.140
You're against me bein' here with youse?!

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:25.740
I'm so sorry!

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:31.280
I didn't know anything about 
you, Zebra-san, so I just, uh...

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:37.860
I got cocky and said that!

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:48.770
His pulse... His breathing... 
He's not lyin'...

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:55.040
In other words, you're sayin' you 
got cocky right in front of me?!

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:59.440
It's been a long time since I met 
somebody this straightforward...

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:04.150
He wasn't lyin' back then either.

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:07.850
Even though he probably 
knew I could hear him...

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:13.190
Figures, he's Toriko's partner...

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:16.330
The punk's got guts.

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:18.660
I'm sorry...

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.360
Listen, kid!

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:26.400
The one act of cockiness I hate more than 
anything else in the world is lyin'.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:29.040
When people say stuff behind 
other people's backs,

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.810
but when they're in front of the 
guy, they're fake suck-ups...

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:34.110
And they get conceited an' keep doin' it,

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:37.610
figurin' they're safe as long 
as they don't get caught out!

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:42.450
I hate those cocky bastards most of all!

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:47.390
I wanna crush every last one of 'em with 
these fingers until they're pulverized!

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:48.720
I-I wasn't...

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:50.590
I didn't lie!

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:54.830
That's what I'm sayin'!

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:58.330
You looked me in the eyes 
and said you got cocky!

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:01.840
I can't remember the last time 
I met somebody honest as that!

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:04.370
Too honest!

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:09.010
You should've tried to lie to 
keep me from gettin' pissed...

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:10.280
Why?!

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:15.080
Well, this time, I'll let you and 
your brass nads off the hook...

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:17.450
Under one condition...

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:18.950
Condition?

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:22.590
Right now, I'm helpin' Toriko out...

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:26.530
...but keep in mind, my reward 
for it hasn't been decided yet.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:33.130
Hey! The camels are all ready!

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.100
Hurry up!

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:41.710
Wow! Toriko-san, these camels...

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.210
Reservoir Camels...

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:48.680
They're giant camels that can store a 
large amount of water in their humps.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:51.250
You can drink water from 
these rare animals anytime.

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:55.920
With all the Zebra hooha, the town only 
had one left, but they lent it to us.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.560
Oh, really?

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:00.530
Zebra-san's is a Wine Camel, right?

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:04.130
That's because I'm an adult!

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:07.470
I can enjoy a snazzy journey 
while drinkin' wine.

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:11.570
And that Eight-Tailed Scorpion 
makes good nibblies.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:13.570
Come to think of it, the woman from town

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:16.010
said we didn't need to return the camels...

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:18.210
I wonder why, even though they're rentals...

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:21.210
Probably because she 
heard where we're headed.

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:25.750
The Gourmet Pyramid?!

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:28.320
We're looking for a certain ingredient...

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.290
Y-You mustn't go!

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:35.190
The Gourmet Pyramid is one of the 
Seven Gourmet Wonders of the World.

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:38.330
It's a place filled with mysteries 
that have never been solved.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:39.730
But more than anything,

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:44.500
surrounding the Gourmet Pyramid 
is a vast maze of red sand.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:49.810
Many Gourmet Hunters have set 
foot in the Desert Labyrinth...

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:52.180
...but none of them have returned...

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:55.780
...so it's also called the Gourmet Graveyard.

00:06:57.620 --> 00:06:58.650
Zebra-sama!

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:01.590
That's a really cocky place, huh?

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:04.790
How about I travel back and 
forth a bunch of times?!

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:07.490
Anyway, hurry up with those camels!

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:08.590
R-Right away!

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:13.060
During the day, the Sand 
Garden is over 60 degrees.

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:17.600
And the place we're heading for 
has mirages and sandstorms.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:21.170
And there are a lot of Beasts 
in the Desert Labyrinth, too.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:24.140
So it's not that we don't 
have to return the camels...

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:28.280
She doesn't expect that 
we'll live to come back.

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:32.880
It looks like this is going 
to be another tough trip...

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:36.990
Hey, Komatsu! Stay hydrated!

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:40.160
Deserts have an extremely 
low level of humidity,

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:42.120
so you're losing a lot of fluids.

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:47.800
Fill your canteen frequently, 
before you start to feel thirsty.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.200
R-Right!

00:07:58.670 --> 00:07:59.740
Here, Komatsu.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:01.640
Thank you!

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:08.820
Something's comin'...

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:16.760
What are those things?!

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:20.530
Sharks that swim through sand! Desert Sharks!

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:32.970
Hey, Toriko. I forget, 
can you eat these things?

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:35.740
No, the meat's too tough!

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:37.750
Can you drive 'em away?

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:40.150
Boring...

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:45.820
Weak Point Voice!

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:05.640
I figured Zebra's voice 
would be up to the job.

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:06.710
Voice?

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:11.840
Did Zebra-san say something just 
now? I couldn't hear anything.

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:16.020
The sharks could hear it. 
It was a sound they hate.

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:19.220
A sound they hate?

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:25.760
Just as we hate the sound 
of scratching on glass,

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:29.400
there are many animals that have 
sounds that they can't stand.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:34.270
Zebra can emit ultrasonic 
waves that we can't hear.

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:36.000
U-Ultrasonic waves?!

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:37.500
He can find, then fire off,

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:40.070
sounds that the Beasts he's facing 
dislike or ones that make them panic.

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:42.040
Wow...

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:44.040
That aside, those sharks...

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:45.840
I'm surprised he chased them off

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:49.280
without killing a single one, 
never mind eating them...

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:51.980
Did he always have this much self-control?

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:38.800
I can see it!

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:43.130
That's the Red Desert maze...

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:46.070
The Desert Labyrinth!

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:50.070
It really is a red desert!

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:54.010
The iron content in the sand 
is oxidized by the sunlight,

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:55.650
which makes it appear red.

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:57.810
That ain't the only reason.

00:10:57.810 --> 00:11:01.120
Beast blood is mixed in with the sand.

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:04.190
Looks like we got to the meat of our journey.

00:11:04.820 --> 00:11:08.720
This is the start of our fun survival game!

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:18.070
W-What heat! It's in another 
league than the desert up to now!

00:11:26.810 --> 00:11:29.740
I had a sample of this kind of 
heat in the Gourmet World...

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:31.980
This is bad... Get hydrated!

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:36.450
K-Komatsu!

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:45.130
Komatsu!

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:48.030
It's quicksand.

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:49.400
A ton of it.

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:58.140
Komatsu's gone somewhere!

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:02.740
I see... So this is the Desert Labyrinth...

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:13.590
W-What the hell is that?!

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.020
A mirage.

00:12:16.020 --> 00:12:20.360
The moment we entered this desert, 
that thing made off with the kid.

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:22.400
Can you search for him, Zebra?!

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:23.930
It's a cinch...

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:27.270
...but using this skill slightly 
puts the damper on my senses.

00:12:27.530 --> 00:12:29.300
So while I'm busy, Toriko,

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:33.210
I'm gonna let you handle them.

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:42.520
So it's finally my turn for some action, huh?

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:00.270
Mirage...

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:02.870
Illusions that appear when light refracts

00:13:02.870 --> 00:13:05.500
due to temperature differences in the air.

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:07.440
Overwhelmingly different air temperatures,

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:10.440
and a large amount of 
impurities in the air...

00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:16.410
Desert Labyrinth makes a cocky, 
maze-like mirage appear.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:22.450
Nature or not, lyin' ain't good...

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:24.960
I ain't gonna let that go!

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:32.460
Echolocation!

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:39.440
Echo Map!

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:44.410
He emits ultrasonic waves

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:47.140
and uses their echo to find out 
the condition of the surroundings.

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:48.580
Echolocation...

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:51.850
It's a skill that takes a 
high level of concentration.

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:56.620
Oh, come on... I still ain't found him...

00:13:56.990 --> 00:14:00.720
Where the hell did you go, kid?!

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:16.470
Five-fold...

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.140
...Spiked Punch!

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:29.590
Well, Zebra? Did you find him?!

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:32.420
He's really far from here...

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:34.460
Far?! Where is he?!

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:38.630
Under the sand. He got 
sucked into the quicksand.

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:39.900
Is he alright?!

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:42.160
For now, anyway...

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:45.270
Zebra... He's restraining his voice.

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:48.040
Is he using his powers to their fullest?!

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:51.810
My guess is he's stretching 
out his map to the limit.

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:54.840
Its maximum range is about 70 kilometers.

00:14:56.440 --> 00:15:01.280
Just how far were you carried, Komatsu?!

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:26.010
Toriko-san! Toriko-san!!

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:32.110
Hey, this ain't good. He keeps 
gettin' further an' further away.

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:36.020
And he's gettin' chased 
by creatures in the sand.

00:15:36.020 --> 00:15:39.750
Can't you do anything?! 
Use sound to help him?!

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:42.120
Shut up for a minute.

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:46.160
I could scatter the beasties by letting 
loose a Howl Bullet from here...

00:15:46.490 --> 00:15:50.360
...but the kid is being carried 
away at a crazy speed.

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:53.270
If he goes outside the bounds of my map,

00:15:53.270 --> 00:15:56.040
I won't have any way to find his location.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.300
Zebra! Let's go after him!

00:15:58.300 --> 00:16:01.640
Komatsu's always prepared for death...

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:04.710
...but he's my partner! I have to save him!

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:07.380
Partner, huh?

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:11.420
Has that kid adapted to you?

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:13.490
Never mind...

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:18.760
We can chase after him, but it means 
takin' a dip into the quicksand.

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:24.030
Desert Labyrinth... Stay 
close behind me, Toriko...

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:45.520
Be careful.

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:49.990
It looks flat 'cause of the 
mirage, but it's actually not.

00:16:50.390 --> 00:16:52.920
Make sure ya stay right behind me.

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:04.530
What's wrong?! You gettin' worn out?!

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:08.810
Aren't you the one who's 
slowed down the pace?

00:17:08.810 --> 00:17:13.340
The hell I have. I just don't 
want you to fall behind, jackass.

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:16.980
Oh, you don't have to slow down for me.

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:19.420
Then maybe I'll sprint ahead...

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:20.880
Whatever you want.

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:23.950
This guy's as competitive as always...

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:29.730
Even back in the day, his pride 
would never let him complain.

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:33.460
Still, this heat and dryness 
is seriously dangerous...

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:35.400
Getting dehydrated...

00:17:37.370 --> 00:17:38.270
What's that?

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:45.010
Yes! A Sandflower Fish!

00:17:50.650 --> 00:17:52.610
We gotta catch it!

00:17:52.610 --> 00:17:53.480
Leave it to me!

00:17:58.450 --> 00:17:59.820
Fork!

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:21.940
I give thanks for this world's bounty.

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:37.620
The sound of Toriko's blood flow has changed.

00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:40.360
Sounds like his blood vessels

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:43.500
have successfully stored a 
large amount of moisture.

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:51.100
I'm adapting...

00:18:51.910 --> 00:18:53.670
...to this environment.

00:18:55.270 --> 00:18:56.940
You doin' okay, Zebra?

00:18:57.510 --> 00:18:58.710
What do ya mean?

00:18:58.710 --> 00:19:01.950
Have you already adapted to this desert?

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:04.450
Adapted? Don't be an idiot.

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:07.950
I already have experience with Magma 
Season back at the Gourmet Prison

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:09.620
and that's about as hot as this.

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:12.760
Did you escape from the prison?!

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:14.830
Just took a walk is all...

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:17.400
Anyway, don't get the wrong idea.

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:22.270
I'm not changin' to accommodate the desert...

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:27.270
The question is whether this 
desert is gonna adapt to me...

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:31.480
Is that right?

00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:34.710
It looks like he's adjusted to it...

00:19:38.350 --> 00:19:44.090
Anyway, if Komatsu is still okay right 
now, this might've been lucky for him.

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:47.020
I'm sure this heat would've 
been hard for him to withstand.

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:48.090
That luck...

00:19:48.690 --> 00:19:50.830
It may be the real deal.

00:19:51.860 --> 00:19:53.230
That kid...

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:57.640
It's like that's where he was 
headed in the first place...

00:19:57.640 --> 00:20:01.040
Maybe he has a talent for 
being drawn to ingredients?

00:20:01.040 --> 00:20:01.810
What?!

00:20:01.810 --> 00:20:05.780
We followed the kid's trail so we 
wouldn't lose him and ended up here...

00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:26.230
That's...

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:28.730
...the Gourmet Pyramid?!

00:21:37.930 --> 00:21:39.230
Dishing with Tina!

00:21:39.600 --> 00:21:42.070
It's "Dishing with Tina", the talk 
show with a heaping helping of fun!

00:21:42.370 --> 00:21:45.910
Our guest today is Gourmet 
Reviver, Teppei-san!

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:48.610
Welcome to the studio, Teppei-san!

00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:51.950
What, are you ignoring me?!

00:21:52.380 --> 00:21:54.480
Least said, soonest mended.

00:21:54.850 --> 00:21:55.820
You spoke...

00:21:56.080 --> 00:22:01.120
On the other hand, I am on a TV talk show, 
so if I don't talk, there's no show!

00:22:01.120 --> 00:22:03.890
The only thing, it wouldn't do 
if I carelessly talked dirty

00:22:03.890 --> 00:22:05.460
and alienated your viewers, right?

00:22:05.460 --> 00:22:07.060
But just between you and me,

00:22:07.060 --> 00:22:09.300
I want to get a higher favorability 
rating than my master!

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:11.860
Oh, that's right! I'm Teppei!

00:22:11.860 --> 00:22:13.370
You talk a mile a minute!

00:22:13.370 --> 00:22:18.270
Alright, let's play Acrostic Corner 
to see what makes our guest tick!

00:22:18.270 --> 00:22:19.640
Okay, I'll start...

00:22:20.740 --> 00:22:21.940
"ReviVE"...

00:22:24.240 --> 00:22:25.280
That's some messy writing!

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:26.180
"VEgetables"...

00:22:26.580 --> 00:22:28.850
I was on my way to buy some, but 
then realized I forgot my wallet,

00:22:28.850 --> 00:22:30.020
so I went back and my Master said,

00:22:30.020 --> 00:22:32.180
"Teppei, also buy this on 
the way!", and I was like,

00:22:32.180 --> 00:22:34.690
"Seriously?! What a pain!", 
but I went and bought it.

00:22:34.690 --> 00:22:35.450
It was a flasK!

00:22:35.450 --> 00:22:38.520
That's too much talking for Acrostic 
Corner! Is this even what you're doing?!

00:22:39.660 --> 00:22:40.730
Kocoa!

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:44.100
Aice!

00:22:44.100 --> 00:22:46.630
When I went to buy some, I realized 
I forgot my shopping basket,

00:22:46.630 --> 00:22:48.870
and when I went back, my Master 
was getting dressed up...

00:22:48.870 --> 00:22:52.770
He said he was gonna be on TV and 
I'm like, "Master, for reals?!"

00:22:52.770 --> 00:22:55.610
Really, I was kinda jealous, but 
after a while, I got invited, too,

00:22:55.610 --> 00:22:56.980
which was really cool, y'know...

00:22:56.980 --> 00:22:57.880
...Tina-paN!

00:22:58.610 --> 00:23:00.310
Can't have words starting with "N"...

00:23:00.310 --> 00:23:02.710
That's insane, losing like that!

00:23:03.180 --> 00:23:04.550
Well, let's move on to the next segment...

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:09.190
A super-sized series of ancient ruins.

00:23:09.190 --> 00:23:11.250
The threat of being trapped forever...

00:23:11.250 --> 00:23:13.480
And Zebra has lost his voice?!

00:23:14.100 --> 00:23:17.060
The Sealed Voice! The Other-Dimensional Gourmet Pyramid!

00:23:17.430 --> 00:23:19.150
Look forward to another heaping helping of fun!
